                <pb facs="0806" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg718"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. McCormick reports that through the cooperation of the Russian Government the
                    Japanese consul at Korsakov has been informed of the permission of the Russian
                    Government for a neutral ship to proceed to that place, and requests to be
                    informed of the name of the vessel and the date of its departure.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
